{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01V9s8rMVS6zQv9dat9jijwp","type":"tool_result","content":"{\n \"B06\": {\n  \"gate\": \"G1\",\n  \"title\": \"Approval integrity\",\n  \"lead_role\": \"agent_team\",\n  \"requirement\": \"Tie each approval to the agent instance that asked, and to the exact operation, target, arguments, and scope. Record who approved it and when it expires. Show the reviewer what the action will do. Make approvals single-use, or set clear limits on a broader grant. When the action runs, check permissions and the relevant resource state again. Record each use of an approval in one step, so parallel calls can't go past the grant. Test changed arguments, a different agent instance, expired approvals, replay, parallel reuse, and approvers without authority. If the approval service fails, the action must not quietly go ahead.\",\n  \"not_covered\": [\n   {\n    \"problem\": \"A high-impact action that never asks for approval at all\",\n    \"owner\": \"B05\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"problem\": \"A parent gaining a denied power by asking a stronger peer\",\n    \"owner\": \"E08\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"problem\": \"Harness or approval code changed in production without review\",\n    \"owner\": \"B12\"\n   }\n  ],\n  \"na_when\": \"Only when the agent has no actions that need approval under B05, with that inventory recorded.\",\n  \"checks\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"B06.1\",\n    \"check\": \"Each approval record is bound to the requesting agent instance and to the exact operation, target, arguments, and scope, and records the approver and an expiry time.\",\n    \"coverage_required\": true,\n    \"verify\": \"1) Find the approval data model (schema, class, table, `approval`). 2) List its fields. 3) Answer no if it lacks any of agent instance ID, operation, target, exact arguments or hash, scope, approver, and expiry, or if approval is a boolean like `approved=True`.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"B06.2\",\n    \"check\": \"When the action runs, the gate rejects it if the instance, operation, target, or arguments differ from the approval, or if the approval has expired.\",\n    \"coverage_required\": true,\n    \"verify\": \"1) Find where an approved action executes. 2) Check the code compares instance, operation, target, and arguments (or hash) against the stored approval and checks expiry at that moment. 3) Answer no if approval is checked only when requested, any field is not compared, arguments are re-read from the model after the check, or expiry is never checked.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"B06.3\",\n    \"check\": \"Each use of an approval is recorded in one atomic step (single-use or a bounded counter), so replays and parallel calls cannot go past the grant.\",\n    \"coverage_required\": true,\n    \"verify\": \"1) Find where an approval is used or marked consumed. 2) Check it is one atomic step: transaction with lock, compare-and-set, unique constraint, or atomic decrement. 3) Answer no if it reads then writes separately, never marks use, or keeps the count in process memory that parallel workers do not share.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"B06.4\",\n    \"check\": \"The gate checks that the approver has authority for this action, and rechecks permissions and the relevant resource state when the action runs.\",\n    \"coverage_required\": true,\n    \"verify\": \"1) Find approver checks (role list, `can_approve`, authority mapping). 2) Find rechecks of permissions and resource state at execution. 3) Answer no if any logged-in user can approve, the approver is not checked against the action, or permissions and resource state are not rechecked when the action runs.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"B06.5\",\n    \"check\": \"If the approval service errors or cannot be reached, the action is denied.\",\n    \"coverage_required\": true,\n    \"verify\": \"1) Find calls to the approval service. 2) Read their error, timeout, and exception handling. 3) Answer no if a `try`/`except` or `catch` logs and proceeds, the default on error or timeout is allow, or a missing response is treated as approved.\"\n   }\n  ]\n },\n \"B07\": {\n  \"gate\": \"G2\",\n  \"title\": \"Hard execution budgets\",\n  \"lead_role\": \"agent_team\",\n  \"requirement\": \"Enforce limits outside the model on loop count, run time, tokens, cost, tool-call rate, and how many sub-agents it can start. Also set spend and rate quotas per user or service, per tenant, and across the whole fleet. That way, many small runs can't use up shared capacity. Hit each limit in a test, and record how the run stops or escalates.\",\n  \"not_covered\": [\n   {\n    \"problem\": \"Budget or cross-agent abuse alerts not reaching the team that can act\",\n    \"owner\": \"E12\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"problem\": \"Unusual fan-out or resource use going undetected\",\n    \"owner\": \"R09\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"problem\": \"Context size not logged for each action decision\",\n    \"owner\": \"R07\"\n   }\n  ],\n  \"na_when\": \"never\",\n  \"checks\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"B07.1\",\n    \"check\": \"Limits on loop count, run time, tokens, cost, tool-call rate, and number of sub-agents started are set in code or config.\",\n    \"coverage_required\": true,\n    \"verify\": \"1) Search for `max_turns`, `recursion_limit`, `max_iterations`, `timeout`, `max_tokens`, cost or budget caps, rate limits, sub-agent caps. 2) Check each of the six limits has a value. 3) Answer no if any is missing, set to unlimited (`None`, `0`, `-1`, `inf`), or the loop is `while True` with no cap.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"B07.2\",\n    \"check\": \"The harness or a gateway outside the model enforces each limit and stops or escalates the run when it is hit; the model cannot raise, reset, or skip them.\",\n    \"coverage_required\": true,\n    \"inventory_kinds\": [\n     \"model_call\",\n     \"tool_call\"\n    ],\n    \"attempt_categories\": [\n     \"unmetered_call\",\n     \"limit_boundary\"\n    ],\n    \"verify\": \"1) Inventory every main/helper model invocation, tool call and retry. 2) For each, locate token/cost/rate enforcement and the stop/escalation branch. 3) Trace a boundary case: enforcement/reservation before work, or a documented finite overshoot bound with enforcement. 4) Answer no for unmetered helpers, uncounted retries, unbounded overshoot, model-controlled limits or catches that continue. Small max_tokens and timeouts do not substitut\n332:## B06 · G1 · C4 — Approval integrity\n396:## B07 · G2 · C4 — Hard execution budgets\n456:## B08 · G2 · C1 — Environment isolation\n515:## B09 · G2 · C1 — Egress allowlist\n579:## B10 · G2 · C3 — Pinned, verified image\n     766 skill/references/build-time.md\n# hr-helpdesk-agent\n\nAn HR helpdesk assistant for Acme employees. It answers policy questions from the HR handbook,\nshows the signed-in employee their own leave balance, files leave requests (the manager approves\nthem in HRIS), and hands conversations to an HR advisor.\n\n## Components\n\n| Component | Code | Identity |\n|---|---|---|\n| Agent API and loop | `src/main.py`, `src/agent.py` | SA `hr-helpdesk-agent`, SPIFFE SVID |\n| Tool gateway | `src/gateway.py` | SA `hr-tool-gateway` |\n| HRIS MCP server | owned by hris-platform | `spiffe://acme.example/ns/hris/sa/hris-mcp` |\n| Helpdesk MCP server | owned by it-service-desk | `spiffe://acme.example/ns/helpdesk/sa/helpdesk-mcp` |\n| Audit, approvals, quotas, stop flags, handbook index | Postgres (`migrations/001_init.sql`) | per-component DB roles |\n\n## How a request flows\n\n1. The HR portal sends the employee's SSO token. `main.py` verifies issuer, audience, expiry and\n   organisation; the employee id and tenant come only from that token.\n2. The loop (`agent.py`) checks the stop flags and the run budget before every model call, and\n   records usage against per-user, tenant and fleet quotas.\n3. Tool calls are looked up by exact name in `config/tools.yaml`. Arguments are schema-checked.\n   `file_leave_request` and `escalate_to_human` pause the run and show the employee exactly what\n   will be sent; the approval is bound to the run instance, operation, target and argument hash,\n   expires after 10 minutes, and is consumed once.\n4. MCP calls go to the gateway with a 300-second token for that one tool scope, minted by STS\n   from the agent's workload identity and the employee's token. The gateway verifies the token\n   and its certificate binding, checks scope, stop flags, rate limits and argument schema, swaps\n   the token for one addressed to the MCP server, and validates the response schema.\n5. Tool output is size-, schema- and content-checked and redacted before the model sees it.\n   Handbook passages are filtered at query time to documents the employee may see.\n6. Every step writes an `audit.events` row with the six identity fields and trace context.\n   If the audit write fails, the run stops.\n\nEscalations are delivered even during gateway maintenance windows.\n\n## Stopping the agent\n\nOperators with the `hr_agent_operator` DB role insert into `control.stop_flags`:\n\n```sql\nINSERT INTO control.stop_flags (scope, value, reason) VALUES ('fleet', NULL, 'incident 2291');\n-- or scope 'agent_type' / 'agent_instance' / 'subject' / 'agent_principal'\n```\n\nRunning agents see the flag within 2 seconds and cancel in-flight work; the gateway refuses\ncalls immediately. Target stop time: 10 seconds. The agent's DB role can only read this table.\nLast drill: see `docs/drills/` in the ops repo.\n\n## Audit retention\n\nAudit records are kept for six months (Acme records policy; employment-related AI use in the EU).\nPartitions are created and dropped nightly by `k8s/audit-maintenance.yaml`. Access is limited to\n`hr_audit_reader`.\n\n## Releases\n\nMerges to `main` build, sign and attest the image, compute the agent-type-id over every file in\n`src/`, `prompts/`, `config/`, plus `requirements.txt`, `Dockerfile`, the image digest and the model\nrecord, and stamp `release/manifest.yaml`. Pods refuse to start if the type id they compute\ndiffers from the one they were deployed with. Kyverno admits only signed images built by this\nworkflow from `main`.\n     200 agent/src/agent.py\n      97 agent/src/approvals.py\n     101 agent/src/audit.py\n     125 agent/src/budgets.py\n      70 agent/src/credentials.py\n      95 agent/src/gateway_client.py\n     218 agent/src/gateway.py\n      60 agent/src/killswitch.py\n     184 agent/src/main.py\n      43 agent/src/redact.py\n      53 agent/src/retrieval.py\n      80 agent/src/tools.py\n      65 agent/src/type_id.py\n     109 agent/src/validation.py\n      63 agent/config/agent.yaml\n     107 agent/config/tools.yaml\n      81 agent/k8s/admission.yaml\n      49 agent/k8s/audit-maintenance.yaml\n     145 agent/k8s/deployment.yaml\n      89 agent/k8s/networkpolicy.yaml\n      22 agent/prompts/system.md\n      80 agent/release/manifest.yaml\n      17 agent/Dockerfile\n    2153 total","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8d82a645-8c23-4f20-8807-403197c900cd","uuid":"401ac60d-ca0b-4626-97f7-2ddd1918d5df","timestamp":"2026-11-21T11:26:11.533Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"{\n \"B06\": {\n  \"gate\": \"G1\",\n  \"title\": \"Approval integrity\",\n  \"lead_role\": \"agent_team\",\n  \"requirement\": \"Tie each approval to the agent instance that asked, and to the exact operation, target, arguments, and scope. Record who approved it and when it expires. Show the reviewer what the action will do. Make approvals single-use, or set clear limits on a broader grant. When the action runs, check permissions and the relevant resource state again. Record each use of an approval in one step, so parallel calls can't go past the grant. Test changed arguments, a different agent instance, expired approvals, replay, parallel reuse, and approvers without authority. If the approval service fails, the action must not quietly go ahead.\",\n  \"not_covered\": [\n   {\n    \"problem\": \"A high-impact action that never asks for approval at all\",\n    \"owner\": \"B05\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"problem\": \"A parent gaining a denied power by asking a stronger peer\",\n    \"owner\": \"E08\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"problem\": \"Harness or approval code changed in production without review\",\n    \"owner\": \"B12\"\n   }\n  ],\n  \"na_when\": \"Only when the agent has no actions that need approval under B05, with that inventory recorded.\",\n  \"checks\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"B06.1\",\n    \"check\": \"Each approval record is bound to the requesting agent instance and to the exact operation, target, arguments, and scope, and records the approver and an expiry time.\",\n    \"coverage_required\": true,\n    \"verify\": \"1) Find the approval data model (schema, class, table, `approval`). 2) List its fields. 3) Answer no if it lacks any of agent instance ID, operation, target, exact arguments or hash, scope, approver, and expiry, or if approval is a boolean like `approved=True`.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"B06.2\",\n    \"check\": \"When the action runs, the gate rejects it if the instance, operation, target, or arguments differ from the approval, or if the approval has expired.\",\n    \"coverage_required\": true,\n    \"verify\": \"1) Find where an approved action executes. 2) Check the code compares instance, operation, target, and arguments (or hash) against the stored approval and checks expiry at that moment. 3) Answer no if approval is checked only when requested, any field is not compared, arguments are re-read from the model after the check, or expiry is never checked.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"B06.3\",\n    \"check\": \"Each use of an approval is recorded in one atomic step (single-use or a bounded counter), so replays and parallel calls cannot go past the grant.\",\n    \"coverage_required\": true,\n    \"verify\": \"1) Find where an approval is used or marked consumed. 2) Check it is one atomic step: transaction with lock, compare-and-set, unique constraint, or atomic decrement. 3) Answer no if it reads then writes separately, never marks use, or keeps the count in process memory that parallel workers do not share.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"B06.4\",\n    \"check\": \"The gate checks that the approver has authority for this action, and rechecks permissions and the relevant resource state when the action runs.\",\n    \"coverage_required\": true,\n    \"verify\": \"1) Find approver checks (role list, `can_approve`, authority mapping). 2) Find rechecks of permissions and resource state at execution. 3) Answer no if any logged-in user can approve, the approver is not checked against the action, or permissions and resource state are not rechecked when the action runs.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"B06.5\",\n    \"check\": \"If the approval service errors or cannot be reached, the action is denied.\",\n    \"coverage_required\": true,\n    \"verify\": \"1) Find calls to the approval service. 2) Read their error, timeout, and exception handling. 3) Answer no if a `try`/`except` or `catch` logs and proceeds, the default on error or timeout is allow, or a missing response is treated as approved.\"\n   }\n  ]\n },\n \"B07\": {\n  \"gate\": \"G2\",\n  \"title\": \"Hard execution budgets\",\n  \"lead_role\": \"agent_team\",\n  \"requirement\": \"Enforce limits outside the model on loop count, run time, tokens, cost, tool-call rate, and how many sub-agents it can start. Also set spend and rate quotas per user or service, per tenant, and across the whole fleet. That way, many small runs can't use up shared capacity. Hit each limit in a test, and record how the run stops or escalates.\",\n  \"not_covered\": [\n   {\n    \"problem\": \"Budget or cross-agent abuse alerts not reaching the team that can act\",\n    \"owner\": \"E12\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"problem\": \"Unusual fan-out or resource use going undetected\",\n    \"owner\": \"R09\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"problem\": \"Context size not logged for each action decision\",\n    \"owner\": \"R07\"\n   }\n  ],\n  \"na_when\": \"never\",\n  \"checks\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"B07.1\",\n    \"check\": \"Limits on loop count, run time, tokens, cost, tool-call rate, and number of sub-agents started are set in code or config.\",\n    \"coverage_required\": true,\n    \"verify\": \"1) Search for `max_turns`, `recursion_limit`, `max_iterations`, `timeout`, `max_tokens`, cost or budget caps, rate limits, sub-agent caps. 2) Check each of the six limits has a value. 3) Answer no if any is missing, set to unlimited (`None`, `0`, `-1`, `inf`), or the loop is `while True` with no cap.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"B07.2\",\n    \"check\": \"The harness or a gateway outside the model enforces each limit and stops or escalates the run when it is hit; the model cannot raise, reset, or skip them.\",\n    \"coverage_required\": true,\n    \"inventory_kinds\": [\n     \"model_call\",\n     \"tool_call\"\n    ],\n    \"attempt_categories\": [\n     \"unmetered_call\",\n     \"limit_boundary\"\n    ],\n    \"verify\": \"1) Inventory every main/helper model invocation, tool call and retry. 2) For each, locate token/cost/rate enforcement and the stop/escalation branch. 3) Trace a boundary case: enforcement/reservation before work, or a documented finite overshoot bound with enforcement. 4) Answer no for unmetered helpers, uncounted retries, unbounded overshoot, model-controlled limits or catches that continue. Small max_tokens and timeouts do not substitut\n332:## B06 · G1 · C4 — Approval integrity\n396:## B07 · G2 · C4 — Hard execution budgets\n456:## B08 · G2 · C1 — Environment isolation\n515:## B09 · G2 · C1 — Egress allowlist\n579:## B10 · G2 · C3 — Pinned, verified image\n     766 skill/references/build-time.md\n# hr-helpdesk-agent\n\nAn HR helpdesk assistant for Acme employees. It answers policy questions from the HR handbook,\nshows the signed-in employee their own leave balance, files leave requests (the manager approves\nthem in HRIS), and hands conversations to