every `image:` field in manifests, Helm values, compose, and Terraform. 2) Check each uses `@sha256:`. 3) Answer no if any production image uses only a tag (`:latest`, `:v1`), or a template defaults to a tag when the digest value is empty.\",\n  \"candidate_sites\": []\n}\n== B10.2\n{\n  \"id\": \"B10.2\",\n  \"check\": \"An admission policy verifies the signature against a pinned key, or a pinned certificate identity and issuer, with no wildcard identity or issuer.\",\n  \"coverage_required\": true,\n  \"verify\": \"1) Find admission policies (Kyverno `verifyImages`, `ClusterImagePolicy`, Gatekeeper). 2) Check the key or certificate identity and issuer are pinned. 3) Answer no if identity or issuer uses `.*` or wildcard regex, issuer is unset, or no admission policy exists. Answer unknown if admission config is outside this repo.\",\n  \"candidate_sites\": []\n}\n== B10.3\n{\n  \"id\": \"B10.3\",\n  \"check\": \"The policy checks provenance fields: builder, source repository, build type, and external parameters.\",\n  \"coverage_required\": true,\n  \"verify\": \"1) In the admission policy, find attestation or provenance conditions. 2) Check builder ID, source repository, build type, and `externalParameters` are each compared to expected values. 3) Answer no if any is missing, provenance is only generated in CI but not verified, or conditions use wildcards.\",\n  \"candidate_sites\": []\n}\n== B10.4\n{\n  \"id\": \"B10.4\",\n  \"check\": \"The policy is in enforce mode, covers production namespaces, and denies images that match no policy.\",\n  \"coverage_required\": true,\n  \"verify\": \"1) Read the policy mode and scope (`validationFailureAction`, `failureAction`, `mode`, namespace selectors, exclusions). 2) Check for a no-match deny. 3) Answer no if mode is `Audit` or `warn`, production namespaces are excluded or unmatched, `failurePolicy: Ignore`, or images matching no policy are allowed.\",\n  \"candidate_sites\": []\n}\n== B10.5\n{\n  \"id\": \"B10.5\",\n  \"check\": \"The pinned Cosign or verifier version is at least 2.6.2 (2.x) or 3.0.4 (3.x).\",\n  \"coverage_required\": true,\n  \"verify\": \"1) Find Cosign or verifier versions in CI workflows (`cosign-installer`, `cosign-release`), Dockerfiles, and policy-controller charts. 2) Compare to 2.6.2 (2.x) and 3.0.4 (3.x). 3) Answer no if any pin is lower or uses `latest` or no version. Answer unknown if no verifier is in this repo.\",\n  \"candidate_sites\": []\n}\nusage: answer.py [-h] [--repo REPO] [--met {yes,no,unknown}]\n                 [--evidence EVIDENCE] [--quote QUOTE] [--counter COUNTER]\n                 [--note NOTE]\n                 [--rating {likely_pass,gap,needs_evidence,na_candidate}]\n                 [--confidence {high,medium,low}] [--summary SUMMARY]\n                 [--next NEXT_STEP] [--violates VIOLATES]\n                 [--also-affects ALSO_AFFECTS]\n                 [--verdict {confirmed,dismissed}] [--item ITEM]\n                 [--reason REASON]\n                 findings {check,flag,item,prescan,next} [target]\n\nWrite one answer into a findings file, check it, and show what's next.\n\nUse this instead of editing the JSON by hand.\n\n  Answer a check:\n    python answer.py FINDINGS.json check B05.2 --met no --evidence src/x.py:41 \\\n        --quote \"exact code on that line\" --note \"what the code does\" [--counter \"what you searched\"]\n\n  Add a red flag:\n    python answer.py FINDINGS.json flag B05 --evidence src/x.py:41 --note \"what's wrong\"\n\n  Finish an item:\n    python answer.py FINDINGS.json item B05 --rating gap --confidence high \\\n        --summary \"one sentence\" --next \"what to fix\" [--violates \"exact words from the requirement\"] \\\n        [--also-affects E06]\n\n  Resolve a pre-scan hit:\n    python answer.py FINDINGS.json prescan H003 --verdict confirmed --item R03 --reason \"...\"","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01V7nBVCgEBaXwJRhQ