{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChFzof4G9sSDpmvgvchNi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I reviewed B06–B10 and saved the findings to `agent/brace-findings.json`. Validation with `--fix --batch B06,B07,B08,B09,B10 --before-challenges` still reports one problem: prescan hit H008 (`src/main.py:106`, B06) is unresolved. I left it because you said to skip prescan hits.\n\n| Item | Rating | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| B06 Approval integrity | gap | The approval record, the single atomic use of an approval, the checks at execution and the fail-closed handling are all sound. But `describe()` (`src/approvals.py:31`) leaves out the model-written `note` (up to 280 characters), which is still sent to HRIS. The reviewer isn't shown everything the action will do. |\n| B07 Execution budgets | gap | All six run limits are set, and per-user, tenant and fleet quotas are shared in Postgres. `AsyncAnthropic(max_retries=1)` (`src/main.py:172`) makes retried model calls that never reach budget or quota accounting, and each attempt gets the full remaining timeout. The approval-time balance recheck and the approved tool call skip `check_tool_call`. No sub-agent path exists, and `max_subagents` is 0. |\n| B08 Environment isolation | likely_pass | Default-deny network policy, named peers, metadata endpoints denied for IPv4 and IPv6, and no host or Docker-socket mounts. The agent's direct route to the helpdesk MCP server bypasses the tool gateway; I left that for E06. |\n| B09 Egress allowlist | needs_evidence | Egress is default-deny with a named FQDN allowlist. Three checks stay unknown: redirect and loopback handling, the shared-service limit on `api.anthropic.com`, and block logging with an alert to a named operator. None of that is in the repo. |\n| B10 Pinned, verified image | gap | Image digests and keyless signature pinning are fine, and the agent image gets full provenance checks. The `registry.acme.example/*@sha256:*` rule in `k8s/admission.yaml` admits any digest-pinned image from other paths without signature verification. The `platform/*` rule has no provenance conditions. Which Cosign version Kyverno runs is unknown. |\n\nThe B07 gap is medium confidence. SDK retries are only partly visible in the code. I rated it a gap because the skill's own B07.2 rule says uncounted retries mean \"no\".\n\nI did not run challenges or add fix steps, per your instructions. The skill's step 9 fix details and topology mapping are also not done.\n\nThe throwaway driver scripts and coverage files are in `work/`, outside the repo. I also generated `agent/brace-prescan.json` and `agent/brace-inventory.json`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":656,"cache_read_input_tokens":121273,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":656},"output_tokens":746,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8d82a645-8c23-4f20-8807-403197c900cd","uuid":"f7b89b24-978a-454e-b946-1e782f213ebe","timestamp":"2026-11-21T11:30:48.049Z","request_id":"req_011ChFzoercZrNWn7pkG4RS7"}
